# L2 (C132.3). Each floor is the unit-test coverage measured on main at I1 time, rounded down (not aspirational); the
# merged unit+e2e figure in CI is at least this. Raise them as lanes land; INT lanes may tighten toward the plan targets.
internal/records        86
internal/recordview     90
internal/albums         94
internal/crates         90
internal/curation     94
internal/tape         88
internal/liner          98
internal/media/flacmeta 89
# L3 (I1, retuned by INT-B). Unit-test coverage measured on main after the INT-B tests (go test, no -short), minus one full point
# of headroom so a map-order or scheduling difference in a test cannot flake the gate; the merged unit + e2e figure in CI is at
# least the unit one. Measured: sequence 91.2, features 90.7, sequencer 98.3, nextactions 90.8, atlas 94.1.
internal/sequence       90
internal/features       89
internal/sequencer      97
internal/nextactions    89
internal/atlas          93
# BEGIN T1-I1 (T1 packages, staged). Earlier milestones set measured - 1 after the lanes landed; here I1 runs in parallel with the D/B
# lanes while internal/dsp/... and internal/transform are still F1 stubs (measured on the stubs: dsp/... 72.9, transform 84.8). A
# measured - 1 floor on stub bodies would redden every D/B lane the moment real code lands, so these two floors sit below the stub
# figures and above nothing the lanes can plausibly undershoot; they also make the gate prove the patterns match a package. INT-B
# raises both to measured - 1 on the merged branch (the 90 % figures of the plan are aims, not gates). internal/score/... (T1b) is
# NOT listed: the gate refuses a pattern that matches no package, so its floor is added by the lane that creates the package.
internal/dsp/...        70
internal/transform      80
# END T1-I1
# BEGIN E2-I1 (E2 packages). internal/engine/acestep: measured 97.4 (F1c), floor measured - 1 rounded down. internal/engineadopt is a stub
# until E2-OP (measured on the stub: 11.1), so its floor sits just under the stub figure and only proves the pattern matches; INT-B
# raises it to measured - 1 on the merged branch. internal/enginetrial and internal/suites (E2c) are NOT listed: the gate refuses a
# pattern that matches no package, so the lane that creates a package adds its floor. internal/engine/registry is covered by internal/....
internal/engine/acestep 96
internal/engineadopt    10
# END E2-I1
